-- UNCONSTRAINED binding sharing the surface name `pick` with cmod's. Its dict arity is 0,
-- independently of cmod's 1 (DICT-SEMANTICS §8 I1).
--
-- POLYMORPHIC on purpose: `s8-i1-samename-independent-dict-arity/`'s shape is monomorphic
-- (`Int -> Int`), so a phantom leading dict is silently consistent there -- define and call
-- site agree on the extra slot and the printed number is right by accident. `a -> a` makes
-- the skew value-observable.
--
-- ⚠️ NOTE WHAT IS **NOT** HERE, and it is the difference from the
-- `s8-i1-samename-unconstrained-poly-callee/` sibling: that fixture's `umod` also declares a
-- `use` helper that calls `pick` LOCALLY, so the occurrence it grades is a same-module one.
-- Here there is no local caller at all. The only occurrence of `pick` in the whole program is
-- in `main.mdk`, reached through `import umod.*` -- a WILDCARD-imported occurrence, which is
-- the one import spelling that contributed no rows to `currentImportDefinersRef` and so fell
-- through to the source-blind bare-name table. See main.mdk's header.
export pick : a -> a
pick x = x
